From 672fcfd1b4a42e652ec45dcd59fae5bb5934865b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 11:55:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Bayes learning-loop key mismatch; persist beliefs across
 restarts

production_harness.py was calling BayesianIntentEngine.observe_outcome()
with intent_signal.queue_chosen (e.g. "billing_queue") while
intent_stats is keyed by the cassette's short intent label (e.g.
"billing"). observe_outcome() silently no-ops on an unmapped key, so
every observation was dropped -- the belief state never changed no
matter how many calls ran, with nothing anywhere recording that this
was happening. Flagged by an independent repository review (24 Jul
2026, commit 67eea1d9), verified directly against this code before
any change was made.

- production_harness.py: pass intent_signal.classification.lower()
  instead of queue_chosen -- verified to match intent_stats for every
  queue the IVR cassette defines.
- queue_staffing_bayes_integration.py:
  - observe_outcome() now logs a warning on an unmapped intent instead
    of silently discarding it (same 'no silent pass' posture used
    elsewhere in this repo).
  - BayesianIntentEngine now persists observations to Redis
    (SENTINEL_REDIS_URL / BAYES_REDIS_URL, same convention as every
    other Redis-backed module here) via a per-resource CircuitBreaker,
    and hydrates its starting beliefs from Redis on construction --
    state now survives a worker restart and is shared across worker
    processes instead of living only in one process's memory.
  - When Redis is unreachable, fails open to the original in-memory-
    only behavior (same exponential moving average as before) --
    single-process, no-Redis deployments are unaffected.
  - get_posterior() computes avg_handling_time as a plain running mean
    of the persisted total when Redis is the shared source of truth,
    not the local EMA -- an EMA can't be correctly resumed after a
    restart or merged across worker processes, so this is a necessary
    consequence of making the state durable, not a scope add.
- Tests/test_bayes_learning_loop.py (new): regression coverage for the
  key-mismatch bug generalized across every cassette queue (not just
  billing_queue by hand), the unmapped-intent logging, fail-open
  behavior with no Redis, and belief state surviving a simulated
  restart via a dedicated throwaway redis-server.
- Tests/test_queue_staffing_bayes.py: existing exact-value Bayes test
  now forces in-memory-only (unreachable redis_url) so it stays
  deterministic now that a real Redis is available in CI/sandbox.

443 passed, 6 skipped, twice back-to-back (438 baseline + 5 new).
ruff (0.15.22) clean, bandit -ll clean.
